From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwqgong-ui <noreply@qwqgong-ui.local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:10:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] system: update the TCP checksum incrementally over the
 NAT rewrite

processIPv4TCP and processIPv6TCP re-summed the entire segment after
rewriting the addresses and ports, so every forwarded TCP packet cost a full
pass over its payload -- and with GRO on the read side that payload can be
64 KiB. The rewrite only touches the two addresses and the two ports; the
length, the protocol and the payload that the pseudo header and the checksum
cover are unchanged, so RFC 1624 eqn. 3 gives the new checksum from the old
one in a few adds.

This is not reachable when _TXChecksumOffload is on, since the checksum is
then zeroed for the kernel to fill in, but that field is package private and
nothing in mihomo sets it, so the full recomputation was running for every
packet on every platform.

Includes a test that checks the incremental result against the full
recomputation over 4000 random v4 and v6 packets.
